<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        Dedicated llama-server (llama.cpp) for the VoiceInk AI-enhancement pass.

        Runs gemma4-e4b permanently on :11435, kept isolated from any swap-on-demand
        model pool (e.g. llama-swap on :11434) so no other model request can ever
        evict it. VoiceInk's Custom provider points here, so enhancement is always
        served by a model that is already resident.

        VoiceInk config:
            API Endpoint URL: http://127.0.0.1:11435/v1/chat/completions
            Model Name:       gemma4-e4b

        --ctx-size 8192 / --parallel 1: single-user; the Vibe Coding prompt alone is
        ~1100-2000 tokens, so a smaller context caused context-exceeded errors.

        FLAGS THAT CARRY THE WEIGHT (see the README "Findings"):

          --mlock         pin the mmap'd weights in RAM so they survive sleep/wake
                          and never re-fault from disk on the first post-wake dictation

          --reasoning off suppress gemma4's thinking-token generation entirely. This
                          is server-side and unconditional; the per-request
                          {"thinking":false} kwarg does NOT stop generation, it only
                          reroutes the tokens to reasoning_content. Without this the
                          model silently "thinks" before every reply and enhancement
                          crawls.

          --spec-type ngram-simple (n=3, m=32) — prompt-lookup speculative decoding.
                          Enhancement is a near-copy task: most output tokens already
                          appear verbatim in the prompt, so drafts looked up from the
                          current context are accepted at a high rate. Measured 2.1x
                          decode throughput (~65 -> ~135 tok/s) on novel dictations,
                          with output BYTE-IDENTICAL to non-speculative decoding at
                          temperature 0 — lossless, no quality trade.
                          Sweep: n=3 beats n=2/4/5; m=32 plateaus (48/64 no better,
                          8/16 worse).

          --swa-full      gemma uses sliding-window attention; without this llama.cpp
                          cannot restore SWA KV state, so any system-prompt switch logs
                          "forcing full prompt re-processing due to lack of cache data"
                          and re-ingests the whole prompt (~1.9s spikes). Matters if you
                          switch prompts per app.

        BENCHMARKING WARNING, learned the hard way: do NOT measure speculative decoding
        by sending the same transcript N times and taking a median. `ngram-mod` keeps a
        PERSISTENT cross-request n-gram store, so repeated inputs let it memorise its own
        output — it looked 4x faster than baseline and is worth 0% on first-exposure
        (i.e. real) text. `ngram-simple` builds its index from the current prompt only,
        which is why it is the one that actually helps. Always benchmark with novel
        transcripts, one exposure each, and normalise against a baseline measured in the
        SAME round — ambient GPU load drifted ~2x between sequential runs here and
        inverted the rankings outright.

        KV cache is deliberately left at f16. q8_0 K/V measured SLOWER to generate
        (1.48x vs 1.64x speedup on an identical spec config — dequant overhead outweighs
        the bandwidth saving at this context size), and at ctx 8192 the memory saved is
        irrelevant on a large-RAM machine. Do not re-add --cache-type-k/v without
        re-benchmarking.

        Paths below use ~ for your home directory — launchd does NOT expand ~, so
        replace each ~ with your absolute home path before loading this.
    -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.user.voiceink-llm</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>~/.local/bin/llama-server</string>
        <string>--host</string>
        <string>127.0.0.1</string>
        <string>--port</string>
        <string>11435</string>
        <string>--model</string>
        <string>~/models/gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf</string>
        <string>-ngl</string>
        <string>99</string>
        <string>--jinja</string>
        <string>--flash-attn</string>
        <string>on</string>
        <string>--spec-type</string>
        <string>ngram-simple</string>
        <string>--spec-ngram-simple-size-n</string>
        <string>3</string>
        <string>--spec-ngram-simple-size-m</string>
        <string>32</string>
        <string>--swa-full</string>
        <string>--ctx-size</string>
        <string>8192</string>
        <string>--parallel</string>
        <string>1</string>
        <string>--mlock</string>
        <string>--reasoning</string>
        <string>off</string>
    </array>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/tmp</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>~/Library/Logs/com.user.voiceink-llm.out</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>~/Library/Logs/com.user.voiceink-llm.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
